  "/convert/png-to-jpg/": "PNG to JPG Converter. Turn PNG screenshots, logos and graphics into much smaller JPG files. Perfect when a PNG is too big to email or upload — same picture, a fraction of the size. TL;DR: Drop a PNG file, get a JPG file back in seconds. Free forever, no sign-up — and your file never leaves your device because the conversion runs in your browser. About PNG: PNG stores every pixel losslessly, which keeps screenshots and logos razor-sharp. The trade-off is size — PNGs are often several megabytes, too heavy for email attachments and quick uploads. About JPG: JPG is the world’s most compatible image format. Its lossy compression squeezes photos and graphics down to a fraction of their size, and it opens on every phone, computer, website and app ever made.",
  "/convert/png-to-webp/": "PNG to WebP Converter. Convert PNG images to WebP, the modern format that keeps transparency while shrinking files by 25–35%. Ideal for faster websites and smaller uploads. TL;DR: Drop a PNG file, get a WebP file back in seconds. Free forever, no sign-up — and your file never leaves your device because the conversion runs in your browser. About PNG: PNG is the default for crisp screenshots and graphics because it never degrades quality. But it barely compresses, so PNG files are bulky — a real problem on the web. About WebP: WebP is Google’s modern image format: 25–35% smaller than PNG or JPG at the same visual quality, with transparency support. Every modern browser displays it natively.",
